**What changed**

- `SettingsDialog` re-based `QDialog` → `QWidget` (`settings.ui` root flipped, button box hand-wired since uic can't target `accept()`/`reject()` on a QWidget). `accept()` saves then emits `closeRequested()`; `reject()` just emits it — the host maps both to tab close, preserving the old OK=apply+close / Cancel=discard semantics.
- `TabWidget::addWidgetTab()` — generic non-web tab host: the page sits in the strip directly, and a read-only `QLineEdit` keeps `m_locationBars` index-locked (`locationBar()` widened to `QLineEdit*` so `currentLocationBar()` never returns null). `currentChanged` gained a widget-tab branch (unbinds chrome actions, titles the window from tab text, focuses the page); `cloneTab`/`clear`/`lineEditReturnPressed` null-guarded.
- `BrowserMainWindow::showSettingsPage(page)` — single-instance: scans for an existing settings tab, focuses it or creates one; `-1` keeps the persisted last-viewed section, deep links force a page.
- All deep links rerouted through `SettingsDialog::openPage(context, page)` (toolbar engines, pop-up settings, manage-containers, command palette) with a standalone modeless-window fallback for callers with no window ancestor.
- Tests: new `buttonBoxCloseRequest` locks the OK/Cancel contract; `dialogSlots` now asserts the tab opens and is single-instance; palette-smoke asserts the deep link opens the tab on the Privacy page.

