## Summary

**Root cause** — not a tab-strip layout bug. `TabWidget::makeNewTabOnProfile` installs the private-badged favicon `QLabel` on off-the-record tabs while it's still empty. Qt's first-show auto-`adjustSize()` snapped it to the empty-label size hint (7×14) and latched it, so the 16px masked badge painted center-clipped — the "half-hidden teal icon" at the strip's left edge. Normal tabs escaped because the loading GIF paints a 16px frame before the label is shown.

**Fix** — one line in the shared `animationLabel()` path in [tabwidget.cpp:2291-2298](file:///home/szefi/Documents/arora-ui/src/tabwidget.cpp): pin new page-icon labels to `16x16` before `setTabButton` shows them. All payloads are already 16px (loading.gif, favicon, private badge). No tor-only code; the strip height already inherits TABS07's bounded `tabSizeHint` — tor strip measures 28px, identical to a normal window's private tab.

**Test** — `tst_BrowserMainWindow::torTabStripLayout` [tst_browsermainwindow.cpp:891-945](file:///home/szefi/Documents/arora-ui/autotests/browsermainwindow/tst_browsermainwindow.cpp) asserts the icon widget is 16×16, visible, contained in the tab rect, the strip respects the TABS07 cap, and tor height matches the normal private-tab baseline.

**Verification**
- browsermainwindow 27/27, tabwidget 18/18, tabbar 11/11, privatebrowsing 11/11
- `make check`: check-warnings PASS; all programs green except the known flake `tst_Dialogs::clearSiteData` (localStorage flush race — passes standalone, unrelated to this change)
- Offscreen grab confirms the full globe+private-mask badge renders unclipped

