## What I found

Auditing the vertical row-height path per spec turned up **no slack to shave**: plain rows already hint at `fm.height() + 8` (a single text line) and `documentMode` makes the production bar non-expanding, so nothing stretches them. I verified that empirically on a real `BrowserMainWindow` — a West strip at 11pt renders rows within the single-line bound, with the container edge stripe and close button intact. The "fat" in the report was the **180px default width**.

## What I changed

- `src/tabbar.cpp` — new `defaultVerticalTabWidth = 140` / `legacyVerticalTabWidth = 180` constants now back the ctor seed, the grip double-click reset, and `reloadVerticalTabWidth()`, which migrates `absent || stored==180` (never-dragged) to 140 while keeping genuine user picks. Clamp 120-400 unchanged.
- `src/tabbar.h` — doc comment updated.
- Tests: new `tst_TabBar::verticalTabWidthMigration` (absent→140, 180→140, 260 kept, 140 round-trip) and `tst_TabWidget::verticalTabCompactDefault` (fresh-profile 140 rail through the real widget, migration + user-set persistence via `loadSettings`); a new real-window vertical leg in `tst_BrowserMainWindow::tabStripCompactHeight`; `verticalTabRows` tightened to a font-metrics bound + `ARORA_TABBAR_GRAB_DIR` grab; `verticalTabResize` re-anchored to the 140 start.
- `ChangeLog` bullet, `.devin/WORKLOG.md`, task row → `done` with evidence in the details stanza.

## Verification

- tst_tabbar 14/14, tst_tabwidget 20/20, tst_browsermainwindow 36/36 — all offscreen `--disable-gpu`
- Offscreen grabs reviewed: compact readable rail, horizontal titles, single-line rows, container stripe visible
- `make check`: check-warnings PASS, all programs green except the known unrelated flake `adblockAppliesOnContainerProfile` (passes standalone — same flake prior runs documented)

One caveat worth noting for the record: the updated spec says the reporter sees rows ~2× a text line; I could not reproduce that on this tree (measured `fm+8` on the real window at 11pt) — the most likely source of remaining "fat" for them would be named tab-group first rows, which intentionally reserve a label band. Stopping after this one task per the loop contract.
