**Root cause** — two defects produced the "dim squeezed sliver":
- `SqueezeLabel` elides by rewriting `text()` in `paintEvent`, which shrinks the `sizeHint()` the menubar's corner negotiation reads (`QMenuBarPrivate::updateGeometries` assigns the corner exactly `sizeHint()`) — one squeezed pass permanently collapsed the corner and destroyed the title string.
- The menubar only renegotiates the corner width when its items are dirty, so a changed title kept the old corner width anyway.

**Fix** in `src/tor/tortitlebar.cpp`:
- New `TorTitleLabel`: keeps the full title, reports the full title width as `sizeHint` (menus move right), swaps the middle-elided form in for display only, tooltip carries the full title — elide adapts both directions, nothing destroyed. Cap raised 360→420 so it claims real room without pushing menus into overflow.
- `syncCornerWidth()` feeds the menubar a geometry pass on `WindowTitleChange` so the new sizeHint wins space immediately.
- Title ink → pure white (~12:1 vs `#4a3372`; correct in both schemes since the chrome stays violet under arora-dark).

**Verified**: new `tst_BrowserMainWindow::torTitleBarTitle` (full short title, capped elide + tooltip + File-menu renegotiation, shrink-back regrowth, near-white ink with zero dark pixels under light *and* dark palettes); suite 37/37; offscreen grab reviewed — bright white "Relay page - Arora (Tor)"; `make check` green (check-warnings PASS, all programs 0 failed) except the known unrelated flake `fileSchemeErrors` (passes standalone).

