**Root cause:** the signal chain was intact — Qt 6.12's `QWebEnginePage::loadProgress` emits only `0` then `100`, never a mid-flight value, so every surface keyed on `0 < progress < 100` was structurally dead (toolbar flip, url-bar cue, `LoadingIndicator` mid-attach).

**Fix — lifecycle-driven, same pattern `LoadingIndicator` already proved:**
- `TabWidget` gains `loadStarted`/`loadFinished(bool)` forwarding the current page's `Engine::Page` lifecycle, re-wired in `currentChanged`.
- `BrowserMainWindow::updateStopReloadState(bool)` flips the combined action (Stop→`m_viewStopAction`, Reload→`m_viewReloadAction`, `Qt::UniqueConnection`); `loadProgress()` still honors real mid-flight values and consults `isLoading()` at the edges.
- New `StopReloadButton` at the url bar's right end (same face rule, click→`stop()`/`reload()`); `LocationBar` paints an indeterminate strip while `WebView::isLoading()`.
- `LoadingIndicator::setWebView` mid-attach now asks the engine instead of the dead progress window.
- Back verified end-to-end: `rootTriggered` dispatches once, one trigger = one history step.

**Verification:**
- `tst_BrowserMainWindow::stopReloadState` (extended): held-open server → Stop face on both surfaces → real stop → finish/fail → real reload → single-step Back → tab-switch → private + tor legs. 3/3 green ×3 runs.
- `check-warnings` PASS (zero diagnostics, clean build). Also fixed a pre-existing `-Wignored-qualifiers` in `scopeshortcuts.cpp` the gate rejected.
- `make check`: all suites green except `torChromeTheme` + `colorSchemeApply` — both documented clean-HEAD flakes, fail standalone identically to prior tasks.

