## Summary

**Root cause:** stale popup geometry, not paint. A shown `QMenu` hosting a `QWidgetAction` never re-lays-out when the hosted widget's `sizeHint` grows, and `QMenu::sizeHint()` caches the open-time footprint outright. Clicking the onion button before the circuit snapshot landed pinned the popup at the small "connecting" size (~222×132) and the full ~350×306 chain rendered squeezed into a sliver showing only flag fragments — exactly the "sometimes big enough, chain lines not viewable" intermittency.

**Fixes:**
- `TorCircuitButton::growMenuToFit()` — resizes a visible menu to `panel->sizeHint() + chrome`, grow-only via `expandedTo` so signature-gated no-op refreshes still touch nothing (TOR13 no-creep preserved). Called on every content/status update path including NEWNYM callbacks.
- `TorChainView::sizeHint()` reserves the standard 5-node chain (browser + 3 hops + site) so size stays stable across circuit rotations.
- Connector pen switched from `palette().Mid` (can equal the window color on flat/high-contrast themes) to translucent `WindowText`.
- Text rects clamped so a squeezed widget never hands `drawText` a negative width.
- Onion button pinned to 20px `iconSize` drawn from a 4× source pixmap; New-circuit button min-height 30px.
- New `torChainView` objectName for test lookup; new `circuitPanelGrowsToFit` regression test.

**Verified:** `tst_tormanager` 17/0/1skip, `--tor-circuit-click-smoke` 60 open/close cycles PASS, `make check` rc=0 (check-warnings clean, 67 programs 0 failed).
