## What changed

The icon-only collapse was confined to `TabBar` — four spots keyed on `isTabPinned`:

- **`initStyleOption`** — cleared `option->text` for pinned tabs → now only `m_iconOnlyTabs` (the TABS09 view mode) clears text.
- **`tabSizeHint` (horizontal)** — pinned tabs returned the `iconSize+20` tile → now get the normal title-driven hint.
- **`paintEvent` (vertical rows + move-drag float)** — skipped re-eliding pinned rows → now re-elides and paints titles.
- **`minimumTabSizeHint`** — pinned floor was the icon tile → now favicon + 5 glyphs + margins, so a squeezed strip elides to a title stub but never goes textless (spec's load-bearing escape hatch).

Everything else pinned is untouched: leading-block position, no close button, middle-click ignored, drag-boundary pin/unpin, session restore, Close-Other-Tabs and idle-sleep exemptions. Rename overrides (TABS12), tooltips and hover previews all flow through the normal `tabText`/`tabToolTip` path, so they work on pinned tabs automatically. Stale comments updated in `tabbar.cpp/.h`, `tabwidget.cpp/.h`.

